            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Croatian Bear"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Flavor was a little bland. Added garlic salt and a little low sodium soy sauce that made it tastier. Love snow peas and the crunch of water chestnuts was great addition.",
            "datePublished": "2018-09-23T14:26:20.290Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Deeli"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Used toasted sesame seeds and, because I don't care for mint, substituted with fresh cilantro instead. Light and refreshing recipe, thanks!! Note: If you sub with cilantro add it at the end when/if you season with salt and pepper because cilantro doesn't stand up to cooking!",
            "datePublished": "2014-10-20T04:38:43.330Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "AnnieM"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My husband loved this, and I ended up liking it, but it had to grow on me. It was fast and easy to make, a big plus. I used half olive and half sesame oil. I think my water chestnuts weren’t the best quality, a little soft. Next time I'll also try toasting the sesame seeds. The mint added a great flavor. All in all a very good recipe. Will definitely be making again.",
            "datePublished": "2009-07-22T19:00:50.250Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Susiema"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I had about 1/2 lb. of snow pea pods that a friend grew in her garden. I sauteed them in sesame oil as directed. When I looked for the water chestnuts - they were not there. Oh well, this would have been 5 star had I added them. I used 1 T. sesame seeds and that was plenty. The seasoning I used was the pepper/garlic and sea salt/garlic grinders. I was pretty light on the fresh mint and will add more next time. It looked really pretty on my plate. A little light soy sauce made it a great dish.",
            "datePublished": "2013-07-05T17:46:53.013Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jackie Taylor"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was okay. The mint flavor was overpowering and I didn't use an entire tablespoon of mint. Next time, if there is one, I would only use a pinch of mint and I would add a splash of soy sauce.",
